Single-database Flask-Migrate repository.

`20260914_01` is a baseline for the schema that existed before Alembic was
introduced. It may upgrade a genuinely empty database. Use the isolated
runner, rather than `create_app()`, while the legacy startup path remains:

    python migration_runner.py --database-url sqlite:///new.db upgrade

An existing SQLite database must be backed up and explicitly checked with:

    python migration_runner.py --database-url sqlite:///current.db stamp-existing

The command refuses empty, partial, changed, or differently-stamped schemas.
It does not run at application startup. The current `db.create_all()` and
manual SQLite startup migrations remain in place until the planned Postgres
cutover.

Do not use `flask db upgrade` during this compatibility period: its normal app
factory still runs legacy schema setup. `migration_runner.py` is the only
supported migration operator path.

The Phase 1 verifier has SQLite integration coverage and PostgreSQL dialect
unit coverage for the equivalent `FLOAT`/`DOUBLE PRECISION` reflection. It
does not yet run against a live PostgreSQL service; that is a required
Supabase staging gate before the production Postgres cutover.
